{"notes":[{"content":{"TLDR":{"value":"We give theoretical bounds for the sample complexity of kernel based RL algorithms under symmetric MDPs"},"venue":{"value":"AISTATS 2026 Poster"},"abstract":{"value":"In many real-world reinforcement learning (RL) problems, the environment exhibits inherent symmetries that can be exploited to improve learning efficiency. This paper develops a theoretical and algorithmic framework for incorporating known group symmetries into kernel-based RL. We propose a symmetry-aware variant of optimistic least-squares value iteration (LSVI), which leverages invariant kernels to encode invariance in both rewards and transition dynamics. Our analysis establishes new bounds on the maximum information gain and covering numbers for invariant RKHSs, explicitly quantifying the sample efficiency gains from symmetry. Empirical results on a customized Frozen Lake environment and a 2D placement design problem confirm the theoretical improvements, demonstrating that symmetry-aware RL achieves significantly better performance than their standard kernel counterparts. These findings highlight the value of structural priors in designing more sample-efficient reinforcement learning algorithms."},"_bibtex":{"value":"@inproceedings{\ncioba2026reinforcement,\ntitle={Reinforcement Learning Using Known Invariances},\nauthor={Alexandru Cioba and Aya Kayal and Laura Toni and Sattar Vakili and Alberto Bernacchia},\nbooktitle={The 29th International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Statistics},\nyear={2026},\nurl={https://openreview.net/forum?id=5InIWpmXwm}\n}"},"title":{"value":"Reinforcement Learning Using Known Invariances"},"pdf":{"value":"/pdf/e9aae264a0e634241b6ed194ffb11bfe6280bbfe.pdf"},"Signed_copyright_form":{"value":"/attachment/20dba940fbc0f6a61f0c882025af016170070fff.pdf"},"code_dataset_url":{"value":"https://github.com/mtkresearch/IQL"},"venueid":{"value":"aistats.org/AISTATS/2026/Conference"},"paperhash":{"value":"cioba|reinforcement_learning_using_known_invariances"},"authorids":{"value":["~Alexandru_Cioba1","~Aya_Kayal1","~Laura_Toni1","~Sattar_Vakili1","~Alberto_Bernacchia1"]},"format_confirmation":{"value":"I agree that I have read and followed the formatting instructions for the camera ready version."},"code_dataset_promise":{"value":"No"},"authors":{"value":["Alexandru Cioba","Aya Kayal","Laura Toni","Sattar Vakili","Alberto Bernacchia"]}},"tmdate":1784233599127,"pdate":1770123850035,"tcdate":1758722755837,"writers":["aistats.org/AISTATS/2026/Conference","aistats.org/AISTATS/2026/Conference/Submission823/Authors"],"signatures":["aistats.org/AISTATS/2026/Conference/Submission823/Authors"],"forum":"5InIWpmXwm","license":"CC BY 4.0","number":823,"cdate":1758722755837,"readers":["everyone"],"invitations":["aistats.org/AISTATS/2026/Conference/-/Submission","aistats.org/AISTATS/2026/Conference/-/Post_Submission","aistats.org/AISTATS/2026/Conference/Submission823/-/Full_Submission","aistats.org/AISTATS/2026/Conference/-/PC_Revision","aistats.org/AISTATS/2026/Conference/-/Edit","aistats.org/AISTATS/2026/Conference/Submission823/-/Camera_Ready_Revision"],"mdate":1784233599127,"odate":1770123850035,"domain":"aistats.org/AISTATS/2026/Conference","id":"5InIWpmXwm","version":2},{"content":{"TLDR":{"value":"Indepently trained models induce changes in the latent representations of the models, but it exists an underlying manifold M where the representations are the same."},"venue":{"value":"TAGML2023 Poster"},"pdf":{"value":"/pdf/add0ada27097a3964361647ea5b1371020db0e17.pdf"},"keywords":{"value":["invariance","latent space","latent comunication","relative representation","zero-shot stitching","representation learning"]},"supplementary_materials":{"value":"/attachment/de16e154a48a04a07586dc6067c86a81fb382290.zip"},"venueid":{"value":"ICML.cc/2023/Workshop/TAGML"},"paperhash":{"value":"cannistraci|infusing_invariances_in_neural_representations"},"authorids":{"value":["~Irene_Cannistraci1","~Marco_Fumero1","~Luca_Moschella1","~Valentino_Maiorca1","~Emanuele_Rodolà1"]},"abstract":{"value":"It has been observed that inner representations learned by different neural networks conceal structural similarities when the networks are trained under similar inductive biases. Exploring the geometric structure of latent spaces within these networks offers insights into the underlying similarity among different neural models and facilitates reasoning about the transformations that connect them. Identifying and estimating these transformations presents a challenging task, but it holds significant potential for various downstream tasks, including merging and stitching different neural architectures for model reuse. In this study, drawing on the geometrical structure of latent spaces, we show how it is possible to define representations that incorporate invariances to the targeted transformations in a single framework. We experimentally analyze how inducing different invariances in the representations affects downstream performances on classification and reconstruction tasks, suggesting that the classes of transformations that relate independent latent spaces depend on the task at hand. We analyze models in a variety of settings including different initializations, architectural changes, and trained on multiple modalities (e.g., text, images), testing our framework on 8 different benchmarks."},"title":{"value":"Infusing invariances in neural representations"},"authors":{"value":["Irene Cannistraci","Marco Fumero","Luca Moschella","Valentino Maiorca","Emanuele Rodolà"]},"type_of_submission":{"value":"Extended Abstract (4 pages, non-archival)"}},"tmdate":1687870974116,"pdate":1687096801933,"tcdate":1686396381157,"writers":["ICML.cc/2023/Workshop/TAGML","ICML.cc/2023/Workshop/TAGML/Submission90/Authors"],"signatures":["ICML.cc/2023/Workshop/TAGML/Submission90/Authors"],"forum":"mCm4iiNoNc","number":90,"cdate":1686396381157,"mdate":1687870974116,"readers":["everyone"],"invitations":["ICML.cc/2023/Workshop/TAGML/-/Submission","ICML.cc/2023/Workshop/TAGML/-/Post_Submission","ICML.cc/2023/Workshop/TAGML/-/Edit","ICML.cc/2023/Workshop/TAGML/Submission90/-/Camera_Ready_Revision"],"odate":1687104356413,"domain":"ICML.cc/2023/Workshop/TAGML","id":"mCm4iiNoNc","version":2},{"content":{"venue":{"value":"CoRR 2025"},"pdf":{"value":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.22402v1"},"venueid":{"value":"dblp.org/journals/CORR/2025"},"paperhash":{"value":"sridhar|mapping_clinical_doubt_locating_linguistic_uncertainty_in_llms"},"authorids":{"value":["","~Raghav_Kaushik_Ravi1",""]},"html":{"value":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.22402"},"_bibtex":{"value":"@article{DBLP:journals/corr/abs-2511-22402,\n  publtype={informal},\n  author={Srivarshinee Sridhar and Raghav Kaushik Ravi and Kripabandhu Ghosh},\n  title={Mapping Clinical Doubt: Locating Linguistic Uncertainty in LLMs},\n  year={2025},\n  month={November},\n  cdate={1761955200000},\n  journal={CoRR},\n  volume={abs/2511.22402},\n  url={https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.22402}\n}\n"},"abstract":{"value":"Large Language Models (LLMs) are increasingly used in clinical settings, where sensitivity to linguistic uncertainty can influence diagnostic interpretation and decision-making. Yet little is known about where such epistemic cues are internally represented within these models. Distinct from uncertainty quantification, which measures output confidence, this work examines input-side representational sensitivity to linguistic uncertainty in medical text. We curate a contrastive dataset of clinical statements varying in epistemic modality (e.g., 'is consistent with' vs. 'may be consistent with') and propose Model Sensitivity to Uncertainty (MSU), a layerwise probing metric that quantifies activation-level shifts induced by uncertainty cues. Our results show that LLMs exhibit structured, depth-dependent sensitivity to clinical uncertainty, suggesting that epistemic information is progressively encoded in deeper layers. These findings reveal how linguistic uncertainty is internally represented in LLMs, offering insight into their interpretability and epistemic reliability."},"title":{"value":"Mapping Clinical Doubt: Locating Linguistic Uncertainty in LLMs"},"authors":{"value":["Srivarshinee Sridhar","Raghav Kaushik Ravi","Kripabandhu Ghosh"]}},"tmdate":1772389986127,"pdate":1767139200000,"externalIds":["dblp:journals/corr/abs-2511-22402"],"tcdate":1772389982965,"writers":["~"],"signatures":["~Raghav_Kaushik_Ravi1"],"forum":"etKkSEWW3u","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","number":842133,"cdate":1761955200000,"readers":["everyone"],"invitations":["DBLP.org/-/Record","DBLP.org/-/Edit"],"mdate":1772389986127,"domain":"DBLP.org","id":"etKkSEWW3u","version":2},{"content":{"venue":{"value":"IEEE Signal Processing Letters"},"venueid":{"value":"OpenReview.net/Public_Article"},"paperhash":{"value":"guo|linguistic_steganalysis_merging_semantic_and_statistical_features"},"html":{"value":"https://doi.org/10.1109/LSP.2022.3212630"},"_bibtex":{"value":"<head>\n<META HTTP-EQUIV=\"Refresh\" CONTENT=\"0;URL=/servlet/useragent\">\n</head>\n"},"title":{"value":"Linguistic Steganalysis Merging Semantic and Statistical Features"},"authors":{"value":[{"fullname":"Shengnan Guo","username":"https://orcid.org/orcid-search/search?searchQuery=Shengnan%20Guo"},{"fullname":"Jianyi Liu","username":"https://orcid.org/orcid-search/search?searchQuery=Jianyi%20Liu"},{"fullname":"Zhongliang Yang","username":"~Zhongliang_Yang1"},{"fullname":"Weike You","username":"https://orcid.org/orcid-search/search?searchQuery=Weike%20You"},{"fullname":"Ru Zhang","username":"https://orcid.org/orcid-search/search?searchQuery=Ru%20Zhang"}]}},"tmdate":1787386219414,"pdate":1640995200000,"externalIds":["doi:10.1109/lsp.2022.3212630"],"tcdate":1787386218893,"writers":["~","OpenReview.net/Public_Article/ORCID.org","OpenReview.net/Support"],"signatures":["~Zhongliang_Yang1"],"forum":"bBAOxjqroz","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","number":99688,"cdate":1665433851229,"readers":["everyone"],"invitations":["OpenReview.net/Public_Article/ORCID.org/-/Record","OpenReview.net/Public_Article/-/Edit"],"mdate":1787386219414,"domain":"OpenReview.net/Public_Article","id":"bBAOxjqroz","version":2},{"content":{"venue":{"value":"IEEE Signal Process. Lett. 2022"},"pdf":{"value":"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/iel7/97/9686799/09913623.pdf"},"venueid":{"value":"dblp.org/journals/SPL/2022"},"paperhash":{"value":"guo|linguistic_steganalysis_merging_semantic_and_statistical_features"},"authorids":{"value":["https://dblp.org/search/pid/api?q=author:Shengnan_Guo_0008:","~Jianyi_Liu2","~Zhongliang_Yang2","~Weike_You1","~Ru_Zhang3"]},"html":{"value":"https://doi.org/10.1109/LSP.2022.3212630"},"_bibtex":{"value":"@article{DBLP:journals/spl/GuoLYYZ22,\n  author={Shengnan Guo and Jianyi Liu and Zhongliang Yang and Weike You and Ru Zhang},\n  title={Linguistic Steganalysis Merging Semantic and Statistical Features},\n  year={2022},\n  cdate={1640995200000},\n  journal={IEEE Signal Process. Lett.},\n  volume={29},\n  pages={2128-2132},\n  url={https://doi.org/10.1109/LSP.2022.3212630}\n}\n"},"abstract":{"value":"With the rapid development of Natural Language Processing (NLP), more and more linguistic steganography methods have appeared in recent years, which may bring great challenges to the protection of cyberspace security. Due to the powerful feature extraction capabilities of Deep neural networks (DNN) to learn semantic features of large volumes of text, traditional steganalysis methods using manual features have gradually evolved into DNN-based methods. However, whether these DNN-based steganalysis methods can extract enough carrier features to achieve efficient steganalysis so that they can completely replace traditional methods based on handcrafted features remains an open question. To explore the answer, in this letter, we propose a new steganalysis method to integrate semantic and statistical features. We use BERT to extract semantic features and TF-IDF with AutoEncoder to obtain statistical features of the input text. Finally, we design a fusion mechanism to combine these two features. The experimental results show that due to the addition of statistical features, the proposed model can significantly improve the detection performance over current DNN-based linguistic steganalysis models."},"title":{"value":"Linguistic Steganalysis Merging Semantic and Statistical Features"},"authors":{"value":["Shengnan Guo","Jianyi Liu","Zhongliang Yang","Weike You","Ru Zhang"]}},"tmdate":1785202651424,"pdate":1640995200000,"tcdate":1739945081624,"writers":["~"],"signatures":["~Jianyi_liu1"],"forum":"5pr8Y10q7X","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","number":327818,"cdate":1640995200000,"readers":["everyone"],"invitations":["DBLP.org/-/Record","DBLP.org/-/Edit","DBLP.org/-/Author_Coreference"],"mdate":1785202651424,"domain":"DBLP.org","id":"5pr8Y10q7X","version":2}],"count":10000}